<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Impact of the Experience Retrieval Mechanism</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This ablation study is designed to isolate the contribution of our experience repository. The first table compares the performance of three model variants across key metrics from HealthBench: a baseline agent with no experience retrieval, an agent using a standard semantic similarity-based retrieval, and our full <span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Doctor-R1</span> agent which incorporates reward and novelty filtering. The results illustrate the performance gains at each stage of the mechanism’s complexity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T8" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:39%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Scaling with Patient Agents</figcaption>
<div id="A2.T8.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:127.2pt;height:49.2pt;vertical-align:-22.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-30.9pt,12.0pt) scale(0.672861589019459,0.672861589019459) ;">
